29 MX c=M | Secret-file ignore rules plus a host-local settings rule.
  t: repository version control
  e: NONE
  r: the reported risk of hiding maintained configuration is not borne out: the patterns match .env files and appsettings.*.local.json, not appsettings.Development.json (read statically)
  - CO SEC-001~ SEC-002~ m=D st=W sr=AM d=WF | .env, .env.* except .env.example, and appsettings.*.local.json are ignored.
  - IA m=D | .claude/settings.local.json is ignored.
30 MX | CLAUDE.md:14 combines instruction-level precedence with an agent duty on contradictions.
  - IA m=MN | Engineering policy lives in the instruction system; a more volatile level may refine but must not contradict a more stable level.
  - XW m=M rel=GOV-018,GOV-009 | When two instruction levels contradict each other the agent reports the contradiction instead of choosing a side.
    s: A Level-2 rule contradicts a Level-1 rule while implementing a feature: the oracle has no rule for instruction-level conflicts (GOV-009 covers only SPECIFICATION/CUSTOM_SETTINGS, GOV-018 questionable requests); L0 requires reporting instead of picking one.
31 MX | Instruction-layer status plus routing of engineering requests from product inputs.
  - IA m=MN rel=GOV-001,GOV-008 | Product and task inputs are not instruction layers and never silently override engineering policy.
  - CO GOV-017~ ARC-020~ m=RA | A product input may request an engineering decision change, which then needs approval.
32 XW m=M rel=GOV-017,GOV-007 | Approval by explicit instruction restates GOV-017; the recording duty is the content, and GOV-007 covers only behavioral rules.
  s: An explicit instruction approves a new library and no decision is recorded: GOV-017 is satisfied; L0's rule is not.
33 MX c=M | Strength vocabulary plus a general reporting duty.
  - XW m=M c=M rel=GOV-005,RUN-009 | A deviation from a 'default' needs a concrete reason and must be reported.
    s: A sound local deviation from a DEFAULT policy goes unmentioned: the oracle's DEFAULT strength allows it; L0's rule does not (C7).
  - IA m=D | must/must not violations are defects; prefer/avoid are guidance; requires approval marks a Reserved decision.
34 CO GOV-001 c=H | Restates GOV-001; the empty template file is the state EXC-001 describes.
